1. Game Overview

1.1 High Concept

LASER CLASH is a fast-paced geometric laser combat game in which two opposing cores battle across a futuristic arena. Both sides automatically fire their primary weapons while collecting energy, purchasing upgrades, and using tactical special attacks to destroy the opposing core.

Players must balance offensive power, defensive protection, energy generation, and special abilities. A player who invests everything in damage may destroy an opponent quickly but risk being eliminated by a well-timed counterattack.

The experience combines the constant action of an arcade shooter with the strategic progression of an incremental upgrade game.

1.2 Core Pitch

Two geometric cores. One arena. Endless escalation.

Build your firepower, protect your core, unleash devastating lasers, and destroy your opponent before they destroy you.

1.3 Design Pillars

Continuous combat

Both sides should always be doing something. Basic weapons fire automatically, ensuring that the match remains active even while players consider upgrades.

Meaningful decisions

Players must choose between improving damage, shooting faster, generating more energy, strengthening their core, or saving for special attacks.

Visible power progression

Every upgrade should have a noticeable effect on gameplay. Lasers become faster or stronger, shields become more visible, and special attacks create dramatic effects.

Readable minimalism

The arena uses a dark background, geometric shapes, subtle grid lines, and bright laser effects. Every important object must remain visually distinguishable.

Accessible controls

The game must work with a keyboard and mouse on desktop and touch controls on mobile without requiring precision input for routine combat.

Expandable architecture

The initial solo game must use reusable combat systems so that additional weapons, AI behaviors, arenas, and online multiplayer can be introduced without rebuilding the game.

