4. Upgrade System

The initial release includes six permanent in-match upgrade categories.

4.1 Damage

Purpose: Increase damage per basic laser hit.

Initial effect: +20% damage per level.

Base cost: 50 energy.

The damage upgrade should make progress visible through stronger hit effects and a larger damage indicator.

4.2 Fire Rate

Purpose: Reduce the interval between automatic shots.

Initial effect: 15% faster firing per level.

Base cost: 60 energy.

A minimum firing interval must be enforced to prevent extremely high firing rates from overwhelming the simulation or creating excessive visual effects.

4.3 Core Armor

Purpose: Reduce incoming damage.

Initial effect: 10% damage reduction per level.

Base cost: 75 energy.

Armor should have a maximum reduction limit. It must not make a core effectively invulnerable.

4.4 Energy Generator

Purpose: Increase passive energy income.

Initial effect: +0.5 energy per second per level.

Base cost: 80 energy.

The generator encourages long-term investment but should not outperform offensive upgrades in every situation.

4.5 Piercing Laser

Purpose: Allow a special projectile or beam to hit multiple valid targets along its path.

Base cost: 100 energy to unlock.

Additional levels may increase penetration count or reduce the ability’s cooldown.

Piercing must not ignore every defensive mechanic. Shields and other protections still apply unless a particular weapon explicitly overrides them.

4.6 Overdrive

Purpose: Temporarily increase offensive power through a powerful laser attack.

Base unlock cost: 120 energy.

The player aims and activates the beam manually. The attack deals burst damage and may penetrate targets.

Its strength is limited by energy cost, duration, and cooldown.

4.7 Upgrade Rules

* Every upgrade has a level, price, and maximum level where applicable.
* Prices are displayed before purchase.
* Successful purchases immediately update the interface.
* The player receives feedback when an upgrade activates.
* Dead players cannot purchase upgrades.
* Purchases cannot produce negative energy.
* Upgrade effects are applied through a shared combat system.
* The AI uses the same upgrade rules as the human player.

