5. Special Abilities

Special abilities create tactical moments beyond automatic fire.

5.1 Overdrive Beam

A concentrated beam deals heavy damage to the opposing core.

* Requires an energy payment.
* Has a cooldown.
* Can be aimed with mouse or touch.
* Produces a bright beam, impact flash, and brief screen shake.
* Cannot be activated while the player is eliminated or unable to pay the cost.

5.2 Pulse Shield

Temporarily protects the core from incoming damage.

* Consumes energy.
* Lasts for a short duration.
* Has a cooldown.
* Displays an obvious shield effect.
* Prevents damage according to its configured absorption rules.

The shield must not stack indefinitely with itself or other defensive effects.

5.3 Energy Pulse

An expanding shockwave crosses the arena and damages the opponent.

Optional secondary effect: temporarily disrupt the opponent’s firing rate.

The disruption should be brief, clearly signaled, and subject to a cooldown.

5.4 Ability Feedback

Every ability must communicate:

* Whether it is available.
* Its energy cost.
* Its cooldown status.
* Whether activation succeeded.
* The effect on the opponent.

On mobile, special-attack buttons must be large enough for reliable touch interaction.

