8. User Interface and Screen Flow

8.1 Main Menu

The main menu includes:

* LASER CLASH logo.
* Play button.
* Game mode selection.
* Difficulty selection.
* Upgrade or cosmetic collection, if unlocked.
* Settings.
* Credits and studio information.

The initial menu should be functional rather than overly elaborate.

8.2 Mode Selection

Available modes in the first release:

* Solo vs AI.
* Difficulty: Easy, Normal, Hard.

Local two-player and online multiplayer should appear only when those modes are implemented and tested.

8.3 Battle HUD

The battle screen includes:

* Enemy health bar.
* Player health bar.
* Energy balances.
* Upgrade buttons and prices.
* Special-attack controls.
* Cooldown indicators.
* Pause button.
* Match timer.

The interface should be positioned around the arena rather than covering its most important combat area.

8.4 Pause Menu

The pause menu contains:

* Resume.
* Restart match.
* Settings.
* Return to main menu.

Pausing must freeze the local combat simulation, including projectiles, cooldowns, AI actions, and energy generation.

Online matches require a different pause policy because one player’s pause must not automatically freeze the opponent’s game.

8.5 Results Screen

The results screen displays:

* Victory, defeat, or draw.
* Match duration.
* Damage dealt.
* Damage received.
* Upgrades purchased.
* Energy spent.
* Rewards earned.
* Rematch button.
* Main menu button.

