11.3 System Responsibilities

CombatSimulation

Coordinates the match state, firing intervals, projectile updates, damage resolution, cooldowns, and win conditions.

Core

Stores a player’s health, energy, upgrades, weapon statistics, and alive or eliminated state.

Projectile

Handles movement, collision, damage attribution, penetration, and cleanup.

EnergySystem

Calculates income, damage rewards, pickup rewards, and energy spending.

UpgradeManager

Validates purchases, calculates prices, and applies upgrade effects.

OpponentAI

Selects strategic actions using the same systems available to the human player.

HUD

Displays the current state without becoming the source of truth for combat data.

Input Controllers

Translate keyboard, mouse, and touch interactions into game actions.

11.4 Simulation Rules

The combat simulation should use a consistent update process:

1. Read valid player actions.
2. Update weapon firing timers.
3. Spawn eligible projectiles.
4. Advance projectiles.
5. Detect and resolve collisions.
6. Apply shields, armor, and damage.
7. Award energy.
8. Update energy income and cooldowns.
9. Evaluate AI decisions.
10. Check match-ending conditions.
11. Update visual and interface state.

The implementation must prevent the same collision or projectile from applying damage multiple times unintentionally.

For online play, authoritative combat logic must be moved or reproduced on the server, with the server determining valid hits and resource changes.

