15. Performance and Compatibility

15.1 Web

The game should run in modern desktop and mobile browsers.

Requirements include:

* Responsive canvas sizing.
* Reliable keyboard and touch input.
* No dependence on hover for essential controls.
* Correct handling of browser resizing.
* Pause or resume behavior when the browser tab loses visibility.
* Efficient projectile and particle cleanup.

15.2 Android

The Android version should use the same game code through Capacitor.

Testing must include:

* Portrait orientation.
* Safe areas and system bars.
* Touch responsiveness.
* Pause and resume.
* Backgrounding and returning to the game.
* Different screen sizes.
* Low-memory devices.
* Performance under heavy projectile effects.

The game must not assume that the browser remains active when the app is backgrounded.

15.3 Performance Targets

Aim for 60 frames per second on supported devices, with graceful degradation on lower-powered hardware.

Use object pooling if projectile or particle creation becomes expensive. Limit unnecessary effects and ensure the game can recover from temporary frame drops without corrupting combat state.

